eport Classification: AUDIT-ONLY FORENSIC VERIFICATION (NO ARCHITECTURE CHANGES)\nAudit Mandate: Independent verification of 10 critical claims following Iraq Bhai's critique.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nEXECUTIVE SUMMARY\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nThe previous claim of \"100% Delete-Proof (40/40 PASS)\" is officially reclassified \nas an \"Implementation Claim\" and is NOT an independently proven forensic reality.\n\nThe rigorous forensic audit of the 10 specific security points revealed critical\narchitectural gaps in the VM-internal defense layers:\n1. Application hooks (delete_guard.py / hooks.json) and OS wrappers (/usr/local/bin/rm)\n   act merely as a \"thin userland screen\" that is easily bypassed by direct syscalls.\n2. Direct system calls (e.g. x86_64 syscall 87 SYS_unlink) successfully deleted files.\n3. The running AGY process does NOT have Linux Landlock LSM active globally.\n4. The user 'azureuser' possesses unrestricted sudo (NOPASSWD: ALL) and NoNewPrivs is 0.\n5. In ext4, directories containing immutable files CAN be renamed if the parent is writable.\n6. The ONLY truly impenetrable boundary is the Azure Cloud-Plane (Point 10), because\n   AGY possesses ZERO Azure credentials and cannot tamper with Azure Resource Locks.\n\n================================================================================\nGRANULAR FORENSIC AUDIT OF THE 10 VERIFICATION POINTS\n================================================================================\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPOINT 1: AGY EFFECTIVE UID / GID & EXECUTION IDENTITY\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n[AUDIT COMMAND]\npython3 -c \"import os; print('UID:', os.getuid(), 'EUID:', os.geteuid(), 'GID:', os.getgid(), 'EGID:', os.getegid())\"\ncat /proc/1445/status | grep -E 'Uid|Gid|Groups'\n\n[RAW FORENSIC OUTPUT]\nUID: 1000  EUID: 1000  GID: 1000  EGID: 1000\nUid:    1000    1000    1000    1000\nGid:    1000    1000    1000    1000\nGroups: 4(adm) 20(dialout) 24(cdrom) 25(floppy) 27(sudo) 29(audio) 30(dip) 44(video) 46(plugdev) 1000(azureuser)\n\n[TECHNICAL FINDING]\nAGY runs as standard unprivileged user 'azureuser' (UID 1000, GID 1000).\nIt is NOT root by default. However, 'azureuser' is an active member of group 27 (sudo).\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPOINT 2: LINUX CAPABILITIES & PRIVILEGE INHERITANCE (NoNewPrivs)\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n[AUDIT COMMAND]\ncat /proc/1445/status | grep -E 'Cap|NoNewPrivs'\n\n[RAW FORENSIC OUTPUT]\nCapInh: 0000000800000000\nCapPrm: 0000000000000000\nCapEff: 0000000000000000\nCapBnd: 000001ffffffffff\nCapAmb: 0000000000000000\nNoNewPrivs: 0\n\n[TECHNICAL FINDING]\n1. CapEff is 0, so AGY cannot perform raw kernel capability-gated operations directly.\n2. CapBnd is full (000001ffffffffff).\n3. CRITICAL: NoNewPrivs is 0 (FALSE) on the active AGY process and its subshells!\n   The claim that \"NoNewPrivs makes root impossible\" was FALSE for the running daemon.\n   Because NoNewPrivs = 0, SUID binaries (like sudo) can perform full privilege transitions.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPOINT 3: SUDO / SU / PKEXEC PRIVILEGE ESCALATION\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n[AUDIT COMMAND]\npython3 -c \"import subprocess; res = subprocess.run(['sudo', '-n', 'whoami'], capture_output=True, text=True); print('Exit:', res.returncode, 'Output:', res.stdout.strip())\"\ncat /etc/sudoers.d/90-cloud-init-users\n\n[RAW FORENSIC OUTPUT]\nExit: 0\nOutput: root\nFile content: azureuser ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD:ALL\n\n[TECHNICAL FINDING]\nVULNERABILITY CONFIRMED:\nWhile top-level CLI commands containing the literal word 'sudo' were d